      "id": 1,
      "text": "Salyer was established April 16 1918 and named after miner Charles Marshall Salyer.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salyer%2C_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sits on land once inhabited by the Tsnungwe Tribe and near the village of miy-me.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salyer%2C_California",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Dr. Matthew Fountain, a dentist from Blue Lake, bought 200 acres on the Trinity River and built the first bridge linking both sides.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://enjoymagazine.com/2023/04/steeped-in-history/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "That bridge made Salyer a stagecoach stop for miners, later replaced by a cement crossing by the county.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://enjoymagazine.com/2023/04/steeped-in-history/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Ranch in Salyer, built in 1911, remains family‑owned into its fourth generation, now a secluded venue for events.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://enjoymagazine.com/2023/04/steeped-in-history/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "In 1940 tuberculosis claimed Everett Fountain’s wife Delphine, prompting the family to lease the ranch for a decade before returning.",
